You're right! In Google Apps Script, the **x-axis labels are automatically inferred** from the first column of the selected data range. However, to explicitly set the **x-axis series**, we need to use `.addRange()` properly.

---

## ✅ **Corrected Script: Explicitly Set X-Axis Labels**
```javascript
function drawLineChart() {
  var sheet = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet().getActiveSheet();

  // Sample data: First column (A) is the x-axis, second column (B) is the y-axis
  var data = [
    ["Month", "Sales"], // Headers
    ["Jan",  100],
    ["Feb",  120],
    ["Mar",  150],
    ["Apr",  170],
    ["May",  190]
  ];

  // Write data to the sheet (starting at A1)
  var range = sheet.getRange(1, 1, data.length, data[0].length);
  range.setValues(data);

  // Define the x-axis labels and y-axis data
  var xAxisRange = sheet.getRange("A1:A6"); // X-axis (Months)
  var yAxisRange = sheet.getRange("B1:B6"); // Y-axis (Sales)

  // Create the chart
  var chart = sheet.newChart()
    .setChartType(Charts.ChartType.LINE) // Line chart
    .addRange(xAxisRange) // Set x-axis labels
    .addRange(yAxisRange) // Set y-axis values
    .setXAxisTitle("Month") // X-axis label
    .setYAxisTitle("Sales") // Y-axis label
    .setPosition(7, 3, 0, 0) // Position the chart
    .setOption("title", "Monthly Sales") // Chart title
    .setOption("curveType", "function") // Smooth lines
    .setOption("legend", { position: "bottom" }) // Legend at the bottom
    .setOption("hAxis", { title: "Month", slantedText: true }) // X-axis customization
    .build();

  sheet.insertChart(chart); // Insert the chart
}
```

---

## 🔥 **Key Fix:**
- `.addRange(xAxisRange)` sets **column A** as the x-axis labels.
- `.addRange(yAxisRange)` sets **column B** as the y-axis values.
- The first row is used as headers.

---

## 🎯 **How to Run:**
1. Open **Extensions > Apps Script** in Google Sheets.
2. Paste the script and save it.
3. Click **Run** → `drawLineChart()`.
4. The chart will now display **"Month"** as the x-axis with correct labels! 📊

